    "done_when": "Every clause of the plan's s13 done-when holds. In reckon/metadata_index.py the shared covered-set reuse _reuse_covered stops being all or nothing and every covered-set reader goes through it: a build with no covered set handed in (the cache-miss read index_rows makes with revalidate false), the revalidate path, and the discovery signature read through _covered_files_for_project and _covered_files. It takes the covered set from the persisted index when one exists, keeps the files of directories whose recorded identity is unchanged, scans only directories whose identity moved plus new subdirectories found in them, and drops the files and descendants of a recorded directory that no longer exists; a project with no persisted index still walks. A new tests/test_a_changed_directory_rescans_only_itself.py persists a temporary nested tree, clears the process cache, reads through index_rows with revalidate false, and proves with its own control each: (1) a non-covered file added to one deep directory leaves the rows unchanged and os.scandir is called for exactly that directory; control: hand build_index no covered set on a cache miss and the scan count equals the directory count. (2) an HTML file added to a changed directory appears, one removed disappears, a new subdirectory's HTML file appears, and each covered set equals a full walk's; control: skip new subdirectories and that file is missing. (3) a removed recorded directory drops its files; control: keep them and the set differs from a full walk's.  (4) a second cold read after case 1, with the process cache cleared again, scans no directory, because the build persisted every directory identity; control: keep the moved directory's identity as recorded before the change and the second read scans it again. (5) on its own freshly persisted tree, after a change like case 1's, _covered_files_for_project scans exactly the moved directory and returns a full walk's set; control: leave it on the all-or-nothing fallback and it scans every directory. Each control is applied, run, logged with its failing id and reversed in a trap, and git status --porcelain afterwards lists only the .venv and .env links. The tests covering the metadata index and covered set pass and so does tests/test_every_module_fits_a_worker_window.py, run with -n 4 at most and a per-run --basetemp; the coordinator runs the population at merge. Every log sits under the run directory with a revision header and ends in EXIT=, on the fleet allocation and not the login node. Write status complete as your very last action and run nothing after it.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Make every covered-set reader take the persisted file set and scan only the directories whose identity moved",
